      See Player","body":"This script is for the AI enemies, to check if they can
      actually see the player, theoretically without looking through walls. (that
      part doesn''t work for some reason.)","colorTheme":"Classic","guid":"a59f01ab-9be2-4b45-b8c6-21a92b884e2a","$type":"Unity.VisualScripting.StickyNote"},{"position":{"xMin":200.6667,"yMin":630.6667,"xMax":362.6666,"yMax":710.6667},"title":"Can
      See Player","body":"If the player is not even in range, the enemy can''t see
      them.","colorTheme":"Classic","guid":"295d9a75-1419-49cc-9376-fb4133828490","$type":"Unity.VisualScripting.StickyNote"},{"position":{"xMin":588.0,"yMin":246.0,"xMax":821.0,"yMax":367.0},"title":"Can
      See Player","body":"Use a raycast to determine if the player is visible. Check
      what the raycast hits to see if it is the player, and if it is, the enemy can
      see the player. However, this raycast doesn''t seem to care about walls. ","colorTheme":"Classic","guid":"f4858daf-1782-4e02-be30-48e8a83be713","$type":"Unity.VisualScripting.StickyNote"}],"$version":"A"}}'
